# The default style sheet.
#
# Every row of the encoding table lives here rather than in the renderer, so all of it can be
# overridden a line at a time. Hues are Okabe-Ito, which stays distinguishable under all three
# common forms of colour blindness — and every difference is carried twice, by shape or by line
# style as well as by colour, so the picture survives a monochrome printout.

# The one declaration the default sheet makes. `run end` is how a document says where the axis
# stops, and without it nothing can ever be *still in flight* — a message arriving after the run
# finished would be drawn as though it had arrived. Every other name is yours.
kind point end kills

style diagram stretch=1.5 axis=linear gap=200 lane-pitch=160 row-pitch=28 theme=light bodies=off

# Structure.
style lifeline        color=#c3c9d3 width=1.5
style lifeline:dead   color=#dbdfe6 width=1.5 dash=2,6

# Messages. The fate is in the line style; the colour only agrees with it.
style arrow             color=#14171c width=1.5
style arrow:never-left  color=#cc79a7 dash=3,3
style arrow:died        color=#cc79a7
style arrow:eaten       color=#d55e00 dash=1,3
style arrow:in-flight   color=#878f9b

# Spans. A span that never closed is torn at the far end.
style span:open  edge=ragged
